---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = '2026-05-02';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for seanreardon.com — GDPR + CPRA-lite compliant."
>
  <article>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      <em>This is a stub. The full privacy policy is being drafted as part of
      the redesign. Per the project's standing GDPR + CPRA-lite compliance
      rule, the published version will list:</em>
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Data collected, by category, with purpose and legal basis</li>
      <li>Third-party processors: Cloudflare (CDN, image hosting, web analytics — aggregate only, no PI), Resend (newsletter delivery via Resend Inc. + Amazon SES), Google reCAPTCHA (form spam protection), future AI providers (Anthropic) when AI features ship</li>
      <li>Retention periods for each data category</li>
      <li>User rights (GDPR access / deletion / correction / portability + California rights)</li>
      <li>How to make a privacy request (the contact form, with a "Privacy request" topic option)</li>
      <li>Cross-border data transfers and Standard Contractual Clauses</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="do-not-sell">Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information</h2>
    <p>
      <em>(Stub. We don't sell or share personal information. Cloudflare Web
      Analytics is aggregate-only; no per-visitor data is collected or
      transmitted to anyone for marketing purposes. The full version of this
      section will explain the right under California law and confirm the
      "no sale/no sharing" stance affirmatively.)</em>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
